   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "marker": "ip",
   "content": [
    "This letter, was written by Paulos and sent to the group of believers there in Thessalonikai (Acts 17:1-10). Paulos had been forced to leave Thessalonikai because there were Yehudim there who got upset about his preaching to non-Jews. So he went on to Korinthos and from there he wrote both of his letters to the believers in Thessalonikai.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "marker": "ip",
   "content": [
    "At that time, the believers in Thessalonikai were confused because there was teaching that troubled them, because they were told that the master Yeshua, the messiah, had already returned. Because they were confused, Paulos blocked that teaching by explaining to them that wars and destruction would come before the messiah returns. The one who brings that destruction is the enemy of the messiah, a miracle-working teacher named the ‘lawless man’.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "marker": "ip",
   "content": [
    "Paulos taught the readers of this letter that it’s necessary to stay alert about everyone teaching them, despite difficulties and sufferings. They need to continue to work for their living and to do good just as Paulos himself had done.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "type": "para",
   "marker": "iot",
